I did not decide any arm this wake. I did find a flaw in how the campaign measures: on page images, the eval gives different answers depending on which node it runs on.

**What I found**
- **Node effect on images.** I re-ran the reference model's plain cell on 300 document questions on node homer-008 (older system image). It scored judge accuracy .623 against .610 for the recorded run. 14 of 300 verdicts flipped (9 up, 5 down), and 57 of 300 answers changed. The recorded run and the earlier identical re-run were both on homer-011. Over 1,500 questions this alone could move a paired difference by about ±.011, about half the campaign's ±.02 noise band.
- **The eval fix from the last wake is not the cause.** Its change only touches the uncompressed reader and adds one check. So I kept it, even though this check missed its ±.01 exact-match limit (+.013).
- **Text inputs look safe so far.** The uncompressed reader gave 300/300 identical answers across two nodes. A compressed text run on homer-008 matched the homer-016 run's scores at rows 710 and 1,110, then was stopped before the end. This is not yet a full-file comparison.
- **The +.037 long-chunk gain mixes node images.** It compares a run on homer-006 (older image) with one on homer-017 (newer image). It is text, so it is probably safe, but that is not proven.
- **First text number (provisional).** The compressed reference model scores .718 on MRQA (1,500 questions) against .807 uncompressed. The biggest gaps are DROP (reasoning) −.20, RACE −.15 and DuoRC −.08. SLURM restarted that job after it had finished, so I kept a copy of the finished file.

**What I launched (8 of 8 allowed)**
- **Arm B (why one long chunk beats ten short ones).** I wrote a builder that first rebuilds the old ten-in-one set exactly (1,500/1,500 rows), then makes three new HotpotQA sets: gold passages joined, distractors joined, all ten joined in shuffled order. One cell per set is queued, each with its gate written down first. The builder's first try stopped itself on a wrong separator and wrote nothing.
- **Two 300-question checks:** one on homer-016 (same image as the recorded run), one on homer-007 (older image). Together they tell whether the image causes the effect or only homer-008.
- **The int8 cell:** I cancelled it while it was queued (no work lost) and resubmitted it on newer-image nodes only. It measures noise, so a node change would corrupt it directly.
- **New rule in the campaign rules (`CAMPAIGN.md`):** image cells count only when paired with a baseline from the same node image. The old "the pipeline is deterministic" claim stays in the file, marked as wrong.

**Other things**
- I fixed the wrong cell count the checker flagged in STATE.md. 17 cells are open now: 7 running, 10 queued. The gpu-be partition took GPUs back from 14 cells today, and SLURM requeues them from zero.
- Every launch needed `--force` because of an expmon bug: it treats any new job as a repeat of a closed test job. I filed that as a gripe, plus one asking for a node column in the grid.
- The next wake starts when the first group of cells leaves the queue, or after 6 hours at most.

Nothing needed from you for the plan. When convenient: clear the old ALERT lines about the failed 01:00 / 01:30 wakes (they hit the account's 5-hour usage limit), and force-add `eval_mm_4b.sh`, `probe_attn_route.sh` and `run_tests_cpu.sh` to git.
